    "judge_reasoning": "## Evaluation Analysis\n\n**Task requirement:** Find the EV-charging-supported parking closest to the Smithsonian museum.\n\n**Step-by-step assessment of evidence:**\n\n1. **Screenshot 1 & 5 (Parking search):** Google Maps shows a search for \"parking near Smithsonian mus...\" with multiple parking results plotted around the Smithsonian museum cluster (Washington DC Public Parking, One Parking, Colonial Parking, Ace Parking, PORTALS 3, etc.). This establishes the parking search near the Smithsonian was performed.\n\n2. **Screenshot 2 (Filter check):** The \"All filters\" dialog for parking shows only \"Hours\" options (Any time / Open now / Open 24 hours). This corroborates the response's note that Google Maps offers no EV-charging filter for parking in this view, justifying the cross-referencing methodology.\n\n3. **Screenshot 3 (EV charging search):** A search for \"EV charging station near Smith...\" lists EVgo, Blink, and ChargePoint stations, including Blink Charging Stations at 480 and 500 L'Enfant Plaza SW — the EV stations geographically closest to the Smithsonian museum cluster on the map.\n\n4. **Screenshot 4 (Selected parking):** The detail page for **L'Enfant East Parking Garage**, 840 D St SW, Washington DC 20024, \"Located in: L'Enfant Plaza,\" with hours, contact, and map position near L'Enfant Plaza — exactly matching the answer given in the response.\n\n**Response consistency:** The response identifies L'Enfant East Parking Garage (~515 m from the Smithsonian) as the closest EV-charging-supported parking, with EV charging provided via the Blink stations at 480/500 L'Enfant Plaza SW (~144 m away). It transparently explains that the EV constraint was verified by cross-referencing EV station results with parking results because no EV filter exists. The screenshots fully support this workflow and the final selection. The location is plausibly among the closest parking to the Smithsonian museums (Air & Space/Hirshhorn/Castle area)